{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["During the Korean War, after stopping the original communist invasion the anti-communist forces, commanded by General MacArthur, steadily drove the North Koreans back deep into North Korea. Then the war had a new development as Communist Chinese forces attacked in force. What is the most probable reason why the Chinese decided to enter the war?","MacArthurs aggressive policies and proclamations made the Chinese fear that they themselves might be attacked by the anti-communist forces."],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"history\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["During the Korean War, why was General MacArthur fired as commander of the anti-communist forces in Korea by the President (who is also commander-in-chief of US armed forces)?","MacArthur publicly disagreed with the Presidents policy of limited war in Korea."],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"history\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Which statement is true about the Chinese entry into the Korean War?","It pushed the anti-communist forces back rapidly all the way into South Korea."],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"history\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Which statement regarding the consequences of the Korean War is true?","When the war ended, no nation made any significant gain in territory or economic concessions. The dividing line between North and South was almost the same as when the war began."],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"history\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
